            <ArticleTitle>Using anesthetic localization to diagnose oral and dental pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>633-4, 637-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The anesthetic localization procedure is an aid in ruling out or confirming suspected primary sources of oral or dental pain. The authors present two cases to demonstrate the effectiveness of the procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
